# Avoid React Native Paper Dialog borders on iOS

## Problem

`react-native-paper` `Dialog` sub-components paint hard-coded separator borders that are visible on iOS:

| Component | Border added |
|---|---|
| `Dialog.ScrollArea` | `borderTopWidth: 1` + `borderBottomWidth: 1` |
| `Dialog.Actions` | Can stack with ScrollArea’s bottom hairline above the action row |

These stack with the `Dialog`’s own shadow/elevation and with iOS sheet rendering, producing a **double-border** or unexpected separator line at the top of action buttons or around the scroll area (classic symptom: Cancel + contained primary button look “boxed” twice).

## Rule

**Never use `Dialog.ScrollArea` or `Dialog.Actions` in this project.**

Do **not** “fix” this by zeroing `borderTopWidth` / `borderBottomWidth` on Paper `Dialog.ScrollArea` as the default pattern — prefer a native sheet so the bug cannot regress when Paper updates defaults.

Instead, build every modal/dialog as a native RN `Modal` (transparent + `animationType="fade"`) with a fully custom sheet `View`:

```tsx
// ✅ Correct — native Modal, no hidden borders
import { Modal, Pressable, ScrollView, View } from 'react-native';

<Modal visible={visible} transparent animationType="fade" onRequestClose={onDismiss} statusBarTranslucent>
  <Pressable style={styles.scrim} onPress={onDismiss}>
    <Pressable style={[styles.sheet, { borderRadius: borderRadius.xl }]} onPress={e => e.stopPropagation()}>
      <Text variant="titleLarge" style={styles.title}>{title}</Text>

      <ScrollView contentContainerStyle={{ padding: spacing.md }}>
        {/* content */}
      </ScrollView>

      <View style={styles.actions}>
        <Button mode="text" onPress={onDismiss}>Cancel</Button>
        <Button mode="contained" onPress={onAccept}>Confirm</Button>
      </View>
    </Pressable>
  </Pressable>
</Modal>
```

```tsx
// ❌ Incorrect — Dialog.ScrollArea and Dialog.Actions add iOS borders
import { Dialog, Portal } from 'react-native-paper';

<Portal>
  <Dialog visible={visible} onDismiss={onDismiss}>
    <Dialog.Title>{title}</Dialog.Title>
    <Dialog.ScrollArea>
      <ScrollView>...</ScrollView>
    </Dialog.ScrollArea>
    <Dialog.Actions>
      <Button onPress={onDismiss}>Cancel</Button>
    </Dialog.Actions>
  </Dialog>
</Portal>
```

## Pattern checklist

When creating any dialog/bottom-sheet/modal in this app:

- [ ] Use `Modal` from `react-native` (not Paper `Dialog` + `Portal` with ScrollArea/Actions)
- [ ] Apply `useSafeAreaInsets()` for `paddingBottom` on the sheet
- [ ] Cap sheet height with `useWindowDimensions()` (e.g. `maxHeight: screenHeight * 0.85`)
- [ ] Use `shadows` from `useTheme()` for elevation — not Paper’s built-in `elevation` prop on bordered surfaces
- [ ] Place action buttons in a plain `View` with `flexDirection: 'row' | 'column'` — no Paper `Dialog.Actions`
- [ ] Paper `Button` inside that `View` is fine; prefer `mode="text"` for secondary and `mode="contained"` for primary

